;;; Commentary:

;; Procedures that observe DOrg's write path over one rich corpus, and the
;; one-shot capture that froze their output at the base revision into
;; `base-golden.eld' beside this file.
;;
;; The golden data is the independent oracle for multi-row insert lowering:
;; it was produced by the base revision's scalar generators, one statement
;; per row, and is never regenerated by candidate code.  Tests load this file
;; for the SAME observation procedures and compare the candidate's output with
;; the frozen values.  Re-capturing is a deliberate act: check out the base
;; revision named in the golden header and run
;;
;;   DORG_INSERT_BATCHING_CAPTURE=<out-file> ./tools/test-scratch run dorg -- \
;;     emacs --batch -Q -L . -L ./tests -L ./lib/mysql -L ./lib/clime \
;;     -l ./tests/dorg-tests-runner.el \
;;     -l ./tests/fixtures/insert-batching/capture.el \
;;     --eval '(dorg-run-tests--batch "^dorg-capture-insert-batching-" t)'
;;
;; Normalization is explicit and closed: Dolt commit hashes become `:commit',
;; temporary store and source paths become `:path' forms, and the one
;; store-local statement (the `dorg_files' binding upsert, whose relative path
;; depends on the store location) becomes `:dorg-files-row'.  Nothing else is
;; rewritten.

;;; Code:

